DOS-PORT (patch 0110, Phase 10 W22-WB-E #44 v3 hang triage). Adds 6
doskutsu_dbg_log sub-bracket lines inside SoundManager::shutdown body
to pinpoint which exact sub-step hangs.

Background -- slot 0108 narrowing 2026-05-07:

W22-WB-E iter showed slot 0108's engine-shutdown brackets fired
exactly as designed and pinned the hang to INSIDE SoundManager::
shutdown:

  engine-shutdown[1/8]: pre-game.tsc->Close   [OK]
  engine-shutdown[2/8]: pre-game.close        [OK]
  engine-shutdown[3/8]: pre-Carets::close     [OK]
  engine-shutdown[4/8]: pre-input_close       [OK]
  engine-shutdown[5/8]: pre-textbox.Deinit    [OK]
  engine-shutdown[6/8]: pre-SoundManager::shutdown  [OK]
  engine-shutdown[7/8]: pre-Renderer::close   [X] NEVER FIRES
  engine-shutdown[8/8]: pre-SDL_Quit          [X] NEVER FIRES

Slot 0110 drills into SoundManager::shutdown body. The function has
5 sub-steps (MidiScheduler::shutdown, Organya::shutdown, Pixtone::
shutdown, MIX_DestroyMixer if _mixer, MIX_Quit) plus a final post-
marker = 6 numbered bracket points. Highest-numbered "snd-shutdown
[N/6]" line in operator's next PAUSESDL.LOG identifies the last
sub-step that completed before the #44 v3 hang.

Bracket points:
  [1/6] pre-MidiScheduler::shutdown
        (slot-0106 method; if hang here -> MidiBackend dtor or
        SDL_DOSMpu401Shutdown / SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown; further
        sub-bracketing into MidiScheduler::shutdown for next iter)
  [2/6] pre-Organya::shutdown
        (Organya synth teardown; if hang here -> singleton dtor or
        SDL3_mixer track destruction)
  [3/6] pre-Pixtone::shutdown
        (Pixtone SFX teardown; if hang here -> track-pool destroy or
        sound-fx buffer free loop)
  [4/6] pre-MIX_DestroyMixer (conditional on _mixer)
        (SDL3_mixer device shutdown; if hang here -> audio-device
        close path; sdl-engine territory possibly -- depends where
        in MIX_DestroyMixer the hang is)
  [5/6] pre-MIX_Quit
        (SDL3_mixer global state unwind; if hang here -> likely SDL
        backend dispatch table teardown)
  [6/6] post-MIX_Quit; SoundManager::shutdown body complete;
        returning to engine-shutdown[7/8]
        (if [6/6] fires but [7/8] doesn't -> hang BETWEEN
        SoundManager::shutdown return and Renderer::close call;
        narrow further next iter at engine-level)

Cross-vendor extern decl for doskutsu_dbg_log added to existing
SoundManager.cpp file-scope extern "C" block (alongside slot 0100's
SDL_DOSAudio* extern + slot 0110's new doskutsu_dbg_log).
SoundManager.cpp's existing extern "C" cluster is the canonical
home for cross-vendor decls per slot 0100 / 0102 / 0103 precedent.

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast):

  Per dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md: DOSBox-X cannot
  reproduce the #44 v3 hang (SB16 DSP-pause hardware-state
  dependency). Smoke validates only:
    (a) compile + link cleanly on top of slot 0109
    (b) all 6 sub-bracket strings in binary via strings-grep
    (c) no init-time regression (engine reaches title cleanly)

  Default smoke: 39 flips, no crashes. Engine starts and reaches
  title; pkill kills mid-run so no shutdown-path lines fire (as
  expected per slot-0108 + slot-0110 testing pattern). All 6
  sub-bracket strings confirmed present in binary via strings-grep.

  Real-HW iter is the essential validation gate -- operator's
  next iter (W22-WB-F or whatever the next iter shape is) Quit
  path will produce numbered sub-bracket lines in PAUSESDL.LOG up
  to the hang point; flush-instr / nx-engine identifies the
  hanging sub-step from the highest line written.

Quality gates per team-lead's dispatch:
  1. [OK] DOSBox-X smoke regression (engine launches cleanly with
     0110 in tree on top of 0109)
  2. [OK] strings-grep verifies all 6 sub-bracket lines in binary
  3. [OK] Other configs regression unchanged
  4. [OK] Patch applies cleanly on top of slot 0109

Iter shape note (per team-lead 2026-05-07): WB removed from next
iter -- operator's photo confirms SB16 PnP CTL0026 + DSP v4.13 (not
the chip variant memory had); probe-engineer dispatching standalone
MPU-401 hardware probe in parallel. WB stays out of operator iters
until probe data informs new SDL approach. Iter shape going forward:
3-PLAY (ORG / OPL3 / PAUSE).

Out of scope (deferred to next iter findings):
  - Sub-bracketing within MidiScheduler::shutdown if [1/6] is the
    last-fired line (slot 0111+: pre-stop / pre-_backend.reset /
    pre-_events.clear)
  - Sub-bracketing within MIX_DestroyMixer / MIX_Quit if [4/6] or
    [5/6] is last-fired (sdl-engine territory; would dispatch a
    SDL/0046+ instrumentation patch)
  - Restoring default-to-auto when sdl-engine WB probe approach
    lands + validates real-HW (one-line revert in slot 0105's
    selectBackendFromEnv)
---
 src/sound/SoundManager.cpp | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
index a3373cc..5303442 100644
--- a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
@@ -36,6 +36,14 @@ extern "C" {
   // storage definitions for g_p10_audio_idle_pause_count_block /
   // g_p10_audio_idle_pause_us_block.
   void p10_audio_idle_pause_callback(std::uint64_t paused_ns);
+
+  // patch 0110 (Phase 10 W22-WB-E #44 v3 hang triage): cross-vendor
+  // extern decl for doskutsu_dbg_log. Declared in vendor/SDL/src/video/
+  // dos/SDL_dosdbg.h with printf-style varargs (per slot 0108
+  // precedent). Used in SoundManager::shutdown for sub-bracket
+  // logging. C linkage matches slot 0108 / 0102 / 0103 / 0100
+  // cross-vendor extern pattern.
+  void doskutsu_dbg_log(const char *fmt, ...);
 }
 
 #define MUSIC_OFF 0
@@ -552,6 +560,18 @@ bool SoundManager::init()
 
 void SoundManager::shutdown()
 {
+  // patch 0110 (Phase 10 W22-WB-E #44 v3 hang triage): sub-bracket
+  // logs for each step inside this body. Slot 0108 narrowed the
+  // hang to between [6/8] (pre-SoundManager::shutdown) and where
+  // [7/8] (pre-Renderer::close) would have fired -- confirming the
+  // hang is INSIDE this function. Numbered sub-bracket lines via
+  // doskutsu_dbg_log (declared at file-scope in main.cpp per slot
+  // 0108) pinpoint the exact sub-step. SDL/0024's per-line fsync
+  // means each line hits disk before the next sub-step starts;
+  // the highest-numbered "snd-shutdown[N/6]" line in PAUSESDL.LOG
+  // identifies the last sub-step that completed before the hang.
+
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("snd-shutdown[1/6]: pre-MidiScheduler::shutdown");
   // patch 0106 (Phase 10 OPL3 hanging-note fix): MidiScheduler shutdown
   // FIRST. Released backend's dtor (MidiBackendOpl3 / WaveBlaster /
   // Stub) fires here in deterministic teardown order, ensuring chip
@@ -564,17 +584,25 @@ void SoundManager::shutdown()
   // KEY-ON -> audible hanging note that persists until reboot.
   MidiScheduler::getInstance()->shutdown();
 
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("snd-shutdown[2/6]: pre-Organya::shutdown");
   Organya::getInstance()->shutdown();
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("snd-shutdown[3/6]: pre-Pixtone::shutdown");
   Pixtone::getInstance()->shutdown();
 
   // DOS-PORT: SDL3_mixer's destroy is MIX_DestroyMixer(mixer); pairs with
   // MIX_CreateMixerDevice. MIX_Quit() then unwinds the global state.
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("snd-shutdown[4/6]: pre-MIX_DestroyMixer "
+                   "(conditional on _mixer)");
   if (_mixer)
   {
     MIX_DestroyMixer(_mixer);
     _mixer = nullptr;
   }
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("snd-shutdown[5/6]: pre-MIX_Quit");
   MIX_Quit();
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("snd-shutdown[6/6]: post-MIX_Quit; "
+                   "SoundManager::shutdown body complete; "
+                   "returning to engine-shutdown[7/8]");
   LOG_INFO("Sound system shutdown");
 }
 
